                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "If you want to get into the Persona series, \n\nPLAY THIS GAME \n\nIt is by far the best one to start of with, purely because it is so easy to get into compared to the rest of the games, it is the most modern in game design and in feel, in writing etc. Persona 3 Reload, while being newer is a remake of Persona 3 from 2006, I played it through including the DLC and while I honestly think it is a better game overall, I do not think it is a better 1st Persona game and I do not think the remake of Persona 4 Golden, Persona 4 Revival will do the job of a 1st persona game better, I could be proven wrong, but at least for now, P5R is the best game to start the series with.\n\nIt has great visuals, pretty funny writing, the characters are quite likeable with the exception of Morgana who is a bit annoying, but even he gets some moments of redemption when he made me think \"you know what, i do not hate you as much as I thought I did\" every character has something interesting to say, everyone of them has some \"demons\" of their own they are trying to deal with and you as the main character learn bit by bit about their struggles, they share their suffering and pain with you.\n\nI genuinely believe playing a Persona game helps you learn to listen to others and their problems. While this game takes place in high school, I honestly think this game is best experienced as an early adult, it just makes you think a bit more about others instead of yourself.\n\nVery much recommend playing Persona 5, even if you play for just 30 minutes at a time or so, just take your time, slow down and have fun, enjoy the experience before you, the game's own loading screen is a flipping drawing of Joker with the text \"Take your time\".",
